{
  "_doc": [
    "Create-a-Skater (src/client/cas.ts builds the skater, src/client/caseditor.ts is the editor: Esc > Character > Create-a-Skater).",
    "A skater is a choice per row (a piece id, or a colour from a palette); cas.ts turns the choices into a kit recipe",
    "(src/client/skater/kitpeople.ts) on the full skater rig, with the attitude's riding style, the special's signature, the",
    "bail and the emote. slots: how many skaters are kept (localStorage soma-skate:cas, each saved as { id, name, choices, kit }",
    "so it reads like a kit recipe); nameMax: letters in a name. palettes: the colours each colour row cycles through.",
    "bodies (girth, belly, bust, shoulder width) and heights (leg length, spine scale) make the rig. Pieces: id, name and the",
    "kit fields they set (hair style, beard style, hat kind and colours, glasses kind, top neck, bottom kind, layer kind,",
    "extra layer kind, prop kind, pattern kind). unlock: a piece is locked until the story's mission is done (story:",
    "a mission id), a sticker is earned (sticker: its id), the Tour career has tapes or goals, or the piece was awarded by",
    "id (cas.ts awardPiece, kept in soma-skate:cas-awards); hint is what a locked piece shows. attitudes: the riding style",
    "(bend, arms, stretch, swing, squash, celebrations, idles, the catch flair and tweak, the face at rest). specials: the",
    "signature flourish in the three specials and their names. bails: the bail style (src/client/skater/bails.ts). emotes:",
    "the taunt and what it says. random: the funny name parts and how often the randomizer goes for a loud combo."
  ],
